<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Pressburg (1805)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1805</span> · Also known as Treaty of Pressburg (1805) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> was signed on 26 December 1805 at Pressburg (Bratislava) between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s victory at Austerlitz. Austria ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> to Napoleon's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a>, Burgau and other lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and Württemberg, which became kingdoms, while receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>. It prepared the way for the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-pressburg-1805.jpg" alt="Peace of Pressburg (1805)" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous 1805-1806 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pressburg_print_1805.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
